### LockGuard - manual requests (VS Code REST Client / JetBrains HTTP Client)
@api1 = http://localhost:8081
@api2 = http://localhost:8082

### 1) Deadlock: send A and B within the same ~1.5 s window (A on api-1, B on api-2)
POST {{api1}}/api/test/deadlock-scenario-a?holdMs=1500

###
POST {{api2}}/api/test/deadlock-scenario-b?holdMs=1500

### 1b) Same race, but the victim retries the unit of work (both end up 200)
POST {{api1}}/api/test/deadlock-scenario-a?maxRetries=2

###
POST {{api2}}/api/test/deadlock-scenario-b?maxRetries=2

### 2) Prevention: opposite order requested, global lock ordering applied -> never deadlocks
POST {{api1}}/api/test/deadlock-scenario-safe?first=account:B&second=account:A

### 3) Three-party cycle inside one process
POST {{api1}}/api/test/three-way-deadlock

### 4) Orphaned lock of a "crashed" process (600 s TTL) -> reclaimed after a few seconds
POST {{api1}}/api/test/crash-simulation?resource=payment:tx-1001&ttlSeconds=600

### 5) Watchdog: 20 s of work on a 3 s lease
POST {{api1}}/api/test/long-running?workMs=20000&leaseMs=3000

### 5b) Same without watchdog -> lock_lost (lease expired mid-work, caught before commit)
POST {{api1}}/api/test/long-running?workMs=6000&leaseMs=2000&disableWatchdog=true

### 6) Re-entrancy + idempotent session id
POST {{api1}}/api/test/reentrant?resource=order:42&depth=3
X-Lock-Session-Id: order-42-request-1

### 7) Contention on a hot key
POST {{api2}}/api/test/contention?resource=inventory:sku-42&workMs=25

### Diagnostics
GET {{api1}}/api/locks

###
GET {{api1}}/api/locks/wait-graph

###
GET {{api1}}/api/locks/events?count=20

###
GET {{api1}}/api/locks/events?kind=DeadlockDetected

###
GET {{api1}}/api/locks/instances

###
GET {{api1}}/metrics
